00downloads/README
2024-Aug-13

If you are looking for latest stable version of the Theory of Computation
textbook by Jim Hefferon, then download the files in this directory.

If you put book.pdf and answers.pdf in the same directory then clicking
on any exercise number in the book will take you to the associated answer,
and clicking on an answer number takes you back to the exercise.  (It is
hard-coded in PDF that they must be in the same directory.)

Also, slides.zip contains the in-class slides that I used when teaching
the class.

Note: a few of the book's diagrams are animated or have opacity.
Some PDF readers don't support these (in particular, the readers that come
embedded in browsers don't support them).  While reading the book works
perfectly well without these features, you may want to consider another reader.
Acrobat Reader supports them and there may be others. 


HOME PAGE

More on this text and my others is at https://hefferon.net. 


LICENSE

The license is that you can use these materials either for self-study or
for a class that you are teaching.  In particular, an instructor can put a
copy on a class's LMS for students to download.  For a complete license
statement see https://hefferon.net/source.html.


PAPER VERSION

See https://hefferon.net/computation/hardcopy.html.